{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pink, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> blue, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> purple cubes that are identical in size. If a cube is selected at random, what is the probability that it is green?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/77302dfbebd642834b52539ec09b25dabf676a38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{9} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{9}{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"362\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the probability that the cube is green, we can divide the number of cubes that are green by the total number of cubes.\n</p><p>The total number of cubes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7469ae9a14972cc30c3772d49500d601ae8486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 + 18 + 9 + 6 + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the probability that the cube selected is green is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57c35cd8601dbc7b7b7577db6a91e8984d165dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{72} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B)} \\frac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"101\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As found in solution 1, the total number of cubes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. This means that the denominator of the results must be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, eliminating C and E.\n</p><p>We can then multiply the other answer choices by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> to check if we get the number of green cubes stated in the original problem. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c7523d7e47cb92c06dcb33cef8daaa23aaca5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B)} \\frac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" /> as the answer.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<t